<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  DiskWise 的 entitlements。

  直发版（Developer ID，非沙盒）在 hardened runtime 下不需要任何 entitlement：
  这个 App 不加载第三方动态库、不注入代码、不起子进程解释器，所以库校验、
  unsigned memory、JIT 这些默认限制一条都碰不到，开 hardened runtime 只是加 flags，
  不需要申请豁免。

  com.apple.security.automation.apple-events (2026-11-06, owner report: "Empty Trash does nothing"):
    Apple documents it as a Hardened Runtime resource-access entitlement — "whether the app may
    prompt the user for permission to send Apple events to other apps". This build is signed with the
    hardened runtime option, so without it the "tell Finder to empty the trash" event is refused and no
    permission prompt ever appears. The earlier note here ("only sandboxed builds can carry it")
    most likely came from testing the sandboxed build, where Finder events are blocked for other reasons.
    NSAppleEventsUsageDescription in Info.plist supplies the prompt text.

  Not here on purpose:
    com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit —— 默认就是 false，写 <false/> 是空操作。

  真要加东西时（比如嵌进一个需要子进程的解释器），往这个 dict 里加对应 key，
  并在提交说明里写清为什么要开这个口子。
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
